msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_MIN <RNGFND1_MIN>` = 0.20 (the minimum range the lidar can accurately report in m)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:78
#: 49cab80536724b8bba13b1b55123a95b
msgid "Connecting via PWM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:80
#: 738f2d51e26e4d86aa811291bab6e6b8
msgid "The PWM interface is recommended because it avoids a number of issues with the I2C interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:82
#: 0b99f35d227944daa3f0c554c3478145
msgid "Connect the Lidar to the rear servo rail of the autopilot and BEC or ESC (to provide power) as shown below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:87
#: a212ff0d31ba4e678ab04cf008e7ab26
msgid "The resistor can be between 200 Ohm and 1kOhm.  Connecting a resistor between the Mode-control pin (number \"5\") and ground (number \"3\") puts the Lidar into continuous acquisition mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:91
#: 9330d150ab25401cb8d57f49a6e414fb
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_TYPE <RNGFND1_TYPE>` = 5 \"PWM\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:92
#: 188d676b27014923a920386d45cd1991
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_PIN <RNGFND1_PIN>` = 54 \"AUX5\" (if using 4.0.0 or higher any Auxiliary output may be used)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:94
#: 1d736817cf9b4816a47a24e250b0dbdb
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_MIN <RNGFND1_MIN>` = 0.2 (the minimum range the lidar can accurately report in m)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:95
#: dab9db39500e4f009394dc47e102d26a
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_SCALING <RNGFND1_SCALING>` = 1 (\"0.8\" may produce more accurate readings for some units)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:96
#: ec401113f6d94bce83a6c45fa32d8030
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_OFFSET <RNGFND1_OFFSET>` = 0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:97
#: 6cc2dcaddd3544cf87063738f9450e14
msgid "``BRD_PWM_COUNT`` = 4 (ensures AUX5 is not used as a servo output)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:99
#: b80020a9ad8649e199fa27c976437f3e
msgid "in firmware versions 4.2 and later, the method for setting a PWM/SERVO/MOTOR output to be a GPIO function is changed. Instead of ``BRD_PWM_COUNT`` being used, the individual ``SERVOx_FUNCTION`` parameter is merely set to \"-1\". If set to \"0\", it remains a PWM output, unassigned to a function, and outputs that output's trim value when board safety is not active. If the servo function is being \"mirrored\" to a remote device, as in the case of a DroneCAN or KDECAN ESC, then in order to change the autopilot board's corresponding output pin to be a GPIO, but allow the ``SERVOx_FUNCTION`` to still be assigned to the remote device, the :ref:`SERVO_GPIO_MASK<SERVO_GPIO_MASK>` parameter can be used to assign the board pin to be a GPIO without affecting the ``SERVOx_FUNCTION`` assignment for the remote device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:103
#: 0141f873577b4bd09344dcb986ca8fe0
msgid "Optional Power Saving"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:105
#: f683005727f34e1fa001d7f74aeac94e
msgid "When using the PWM driver you can optionally configure the lidar to be disabled when the vehicle is more than a specified height above the terrain (using SRTM altitudes) saving about 100mA of current."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:112
#: 2bc2d0b1d2434885aa133ccca6d01c01
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_STOP_PIN <RNGFND1_STOP_PIN>` to 55 \"AUX6\" (other auxiliary pins may also be used)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:113
#: 540f27a99fe542818a48f4f904083355
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_PWRRNG <RNGFND1_PWRRNG>` to a terrain height in meters above which the Lidar will be disabled to save power"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:115
#: b8c6683cbc8f4c629064d2ee46010d61
msgid "When the terrain data indicates that the vehicle is above the :ref:`RNGFND1_PWRRNG <RNGFND1_PWRRNG>` height the :ref:`RNGFND1_STOP_PIN <RNGFND1_STOP_PIN>` will be used to disable the Lidar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:118
#: 98c562c744a841c0b6afcdfad93bc153
msgid "Your GCS must :ref:`provide terrain data <common-terrain-following>` for this to work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:122
#: 46171e97485d4fbe9473e0ef60ac08be
msgid "Testing the sensor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:124
#: 77f49160769a4cab8f4fb6a9e00cf0b6
msgid "Distances read by the sensor can be seen in the Mission Planner's Flight Data screen's Status tab.  Look closely for \"rangefinder1\". It's best to place the Lidar several known distances (1m, 3m, 5m) from a large flat wall to test it.  If the Lidar is constantly reading wrong by a fixed offset e.g. it's always 50cm out at each distance then adjust the ``RNGFNDx_OFFSET`` parameter by the correct amount.  If however it gets the distance wrong each time by a different amount then the ``RNGFNDx_SCALING`` parameter needs changing.  Update it (maybe 1.1 or 0.9) and test again and repeat until it's correct."
msgstr ""

